WEBVTT

00:09.384 --> 00:10.552
Eleven.

00:10.927 --> 00:12.595
Mike. [gasps]

00:16.599 --> 00:17.767
Is that...

00:22.981 --> 00:24.399
I never gave up on you.

00:25.442 --> 00:28.361
I called you every night.
Every night for--

00:28.445 --> 00:29.904
353 days.

00:31.823 --> 00:32.991
I heard.

00:33.700 --> 00:35.452
Why didn't you tell me you were there?

00:35.535 --> 00:37.787
- That you were okay?
- [Hopper] Because I wouldn't let her.

00:41.499 --> 00:43.835
- The hell is this? Where you been?
- Where have you been?

00:45.587 --> 00:46.796
You've been hiding her.

00:48.631 --> 00:50.550
- You've been hiding her this whole time!
- Hey!

00:51.134 --> 00:52.635
Let's talk.

00:53.553 --> 00:54.637
Alone.

00:59.642 --> 01:03.313
- Protecting her! Protecting her?
- Listen. Listen to me.

01:03.396 --> 01:05.690
The more people know about her,
the more danger she's in.

01:05.774 --> 01:07.984
And the more danger
you and your family are in--

01:08.068 --> 01:09.360
So I should be thanking you?

01:09.444 --> 01:13.031
I'm not asking you to thank me!
I'm asking you to try to understand.

01:13.114 --> 01:14.449
I don't! I don't understand!

01:14.532 --> 01:17.368
That's fine. That's fine!
Just do not blame her!

01:17.452 --> 01:19.329
All right? She's upset enough as it is.

01:19.412 --> 01:21.790
I don't blame her! I blame you!
I blame you!

01:21.873 --> 01:24.083
That's okay, kid. That's okay.

01:24.167 --> 01:26.294
No! Nothing about this is okay!

01:26.377 --> 01:28.922
- Nothing about this is okay!
- Oh, jeez--

01:29.005 --> 01:30.673
You're a stupid, disgusting,

01:30.757 --> 01:32.634
- lying piece of shit!
- Okay. All right! Stop it.

01:32.717 --> 01:34.636
- Liar! Liar! Liar!
- Stop it. It's okay.

01:34.719 --> 01:37.305
- Stop it! Stop it!
- [crying] Liar! Liar!

01:41.518 --> 01:45.063
You're okay, kid. You're okay.

01:47.816 --> 01:49.359
I'm sorry, kid.

01:52.403 --> 01:54.823
- [Lucas] We missed you.
- I missed you, too.

01:54.906 --> 01:56.991
[Dustin] We talked about you
pretty much every day.

02:02.247 --> 02:03.456
Teeth.

02:03.540 --> 02:05.208
- What?
- You have teeth.

02:06.084 --> 02:09.712
Oh. You like these pearls? [purrs]

02:10.130 --> 02:11.422
[Max] Eleven?

02:13.466 --> 02:16.553
Hey. Um, I'm Max.

02:16.636 --> 02:17.971
I've heard a lot about you.

02:22.183 --> 02:25.311
- [sighs] Hey. Hey, sweetheart.
- [cries]

02:26.604 --> 02:28.565
[sniffles] Hey.

02:30.817 --> 02:32.068
Can I see him?

02:34.279 --> 02:35.280
[sighs]

02:46.457 --> 02:48.543
He's not doing well.

02:51.629 --> 02:53.006
I know.

02:55.091 --> 02:56.384
I saw.

02:57.260 --> 02:58.928
What else did you see?

03:11.316 --> 03:13.985
You opened this gate before, right?

03:16.821 --> 03:18.156
Yes.

03:20.491 --> 03:24.454
Do you think if we got you back there,
that you could close it?

03:43.681 --> 03:45.934
[roars and screeches]

03:48.895 --> 03:50.647
[theme music playing]

04:55.003 --> 04:59.215
♪ Memories ♪

04:59.299 --> 05:05.722
♪ Light the corners of my mind ♪

05:06.806 --> 05:07.932
[doorbell rings]

05:08.016 --> 05:13.604
♪ Misty water-colored memories ♪

05:13.688 --> 05:16.232
- [doorbell rings]
- ♪ Of the way we were ♪

05:16.316 --> 05:18.985
Ted! Would you please get that?

05:19.652 --> 05:20.695
[snoring]

05:20.778 --> 05:22.530
[doorbell continues ringing]

05:27.869 --> 05:30.455
- [doorbell continues ringing]
- Ted!

05:30.538 --> 05:32.332
♪ Of the smiles we left behind ♪

05:32.415 --> 05:34.876
[doorbell ringing rapidly]

05:38.046 --> 05:39.922
Hold on, please.

05:43.760 --> 05:46.512
- Oh. Hi.
- Hi.

05:47.889 --> 05:50.224
I, uh, didn't realize Nancy had a sister.

05:50.308 --> 05:51.309
[chuckles]

05:52.560 --> 05:53.394
What's so funny?

05:54.520 --> 05:55.563
I'm Nancy's mother.

05:56.147 --> 05:57.440
- No.
- Yes. [chuckles]

05:57.523 --> 05:59.275
Mrs. Wheeler.

05:59.358 --> 06:01.444
[stammers] Um, I'm sorry, and you are?

06:02.028 --> 06:04.280
Billy. Billy Hargrove.

06:06.115 --> 06:07.533
You must be here for Nancy.

06:07.617 --> 06:10.495
Nancy? No, no, no. Not my type. Uh...

06:10.578 --> 06:14.624
No, actually,
I am looking for my little sister Max.

06:14.707 --> 06:16.334
Goes by Maxine.

06:16.417 --> 06:19.462
She's been missing all day,
and, uh, to be honest with you,

06:19.545 --> 06:22.465
- I've been worried sick, you know, so...
- Oh.

06:22.548 --> 06:26.594
I thought she was at Lucas', but
Mrs. Sinclair said your house is the...

06:27.762 --> 06:30.431
the designated hangout, so, you know...

06:32.975 --> 06:34.143
Here I am.

06:36.145 --> 06:39.732
Their driveway is pretty dark
this time of night.

06:40.942 --> 06:42.110
So drive slowly.

06:44.445 --> 06:45.321
Always.

06:45.404 --> 06:47.990
And when you see Mike,
tell him to come home already, okay?

06:48.074 --> 06:49.867
You're a real lifesaver, you know that?

06:51.994 --> 06:52.995
Anytime.

06:53.079 --> 06:55.206
- ♪ Do believe it ♪
- I'll see you later.

06:57.458 --> 07:01.379
♪ Do believe that I'm falling in love ♪

07:01.462 --> 07:02.880
- Hmm.
- ♪ Do believe it ♪

07:05.383 --> 07:09.220
♪ Do believe that I'm falling in love ♪

07:09.303 --> 07:10.888
♪ Do believe it ♪

07:13.266 --> 07:16.978
♪ Do believe that I'm falling in love ♪

07:20.106 --> 07:22.984
[Hopper sighs]
It's not like it was before. It's grown.

07:23.067 --> 07:26.446
A lot. And, I mean,
that's considering we can get in there.

07:26.529 --> 07:28.281
The place is crawling with those dogs.

07:28.364 --> 07:29.240
Demo-dogs.

07:29.323 --> 07:34.036
- [sighs] I'm sorry, what?
- I said, uh, Demo-dogs.

07:34.120 --> 07:35.621
Like Demogorgon and dogs.

07:35.705 --> 07:37.623
You put them together,
it sounds pretty badass--

07:37.707 --> 07:38.958
How is this important right now?

07:39.041 --> 07:40.376
It's not. I'm sorry.

07:40.460 --> 07:41.419
I can do it.

07:42.587 --> 07:43.504
You're not hearing me.

07:43.588 --> 07:45.923
I'm hearing you. I can do it.

07:46.007 --> 07:48.384
Even if El can,
there's still another problem.

07:48.468 --> 07:51.304
- If the brain dies, the body dies.
- I thought that was the whole point.

07:51.387 --> 07:54.056
It is,
but if we're really right about this...

07:54.140 --> 07:57.185
I mean, if El closes the gate
and kills the mind flayer's army...

07:57.268 --> 07:58.686
Will's a part of that army.

07:58.769 --> 08:00.354
Closing the gate will kill him.

08:13.993 --> 08:16.245
- [Joyce] He likes it cold.
- [Hopper] What?

08:17.288 --> 08:19.290
It's what Will kept saying to me.

08:20.583 --> 08:21.792
He likes it cold.

08:24.462 --> 08:26.047
We keep giving it what it wants.

08:26.130 --> 08:30.843
If this is a virus,
and Will's the host, then...

08:30.927 --> 08:32.929
Then we need
to make the host uninhabitable.

08:33.763 --> 08:35.515
[Nancy] So if he likes it cold...

08:35.598 --> 08:36.974
We need to burn it out of him.

08:37.058 --> 08:39.185
We have to do it somewhere
he doesn't know this time.

08:39.268 --> 08:40.603
Yeah, somewhere far away.

08:43.272 --> 08:47.193
Take Denfield,
then you'll see a large oak tree.

08:47.276 --> 08:50.655
You're gonna swing a right.
That road is gonna dead-end.

08:50.738 --> 08:53.074
And it's about a five-minute walk
from there.

08:53.157 --> 08:56.953
[panting] Okay. Denfield to oak tree.
Swing a right.

08:57.036 --> 08:59.205
That's it. But it's channel ten, right?

08:59.288 --> 09:00.957
It's channel ten. Listen...

09:01.040 --> 09:03.793
You let me know
when that thing is out of him.

09:14.178 --> 09:15.429
You should go with him.

09:17.265 --> 09:19.141
- What?
- With Jonathan.

09:19.767 --> 09:22.979
No, I'm...
[scoffs] I'm not just gonna leave Mike.

09:24.021 --> 09:25.398
No one's leaving anyone.

09:27.400 --> 09:32.113
I may be a pretty shitty boyfriend,
but...

09:34.156 --> 09:36.826
turns out I'm actually
a pretty damn good babysitter.

09:45.626 --> 09:46.752
Steve...

09:46.836 --> 09:48.087
It's okay, Nance.

09:50.464 --> 09:51.299
It's okay.

09:52.758 --> 09:53.759
I...

10:05.438 --> 10:08.816
Just be careful, okay?
I can't lose you again.

10:09.942 --> 10:11.611
You won't lose me.

10:12.445 --> 10:13.404
Do you promise?

10:14.697 --> 10:15.698
Promise.

10:20.286 --> 10:23.247
El... Come on, let's go. It's time.

10:25.791 --> 10:26.709
[sighs deeply]

10:27.251 --> 10:28.085
Okay.

10:32.882 --> 10:34.508
[engine starts]

11:18.803 --> 11:20.846
So, what, we're just
not gonna talk about it, huh?

11:22.014 --> 11:23.557
About what?

11:23.891 --> 11:25.643
Oh, I don't know.
I'm just curious, you know,

11:25.726 --> 11:28.396
why all of a sudden
you look like some kind of MTV punk.

11:31.440 --> 11:34.777
I'm not mad, kid. I just want to know
where you've been.

11:36.654 --> 11:37.655
That's all.

11:40.533 --> 11:42.076
To see Mama.

11:44.829 --> 11:46.205
Okay.

11:48.833 --> 11:50.710
- How'd you get there?
- A truck.

11:50.793 --> 11:51.836
A truck?

11:52.420 --> 11:53.462
A big truck.

11:54.588 --> 11:57.007
A big truck? Whose truck was it?

11:57.091 --> 11:58.926
- A man's.
- A man's?

11:59.427 --> 12:00.469
A nice man.

12:02.721 --> 12:05.766
Okay. So let me just
get this straight in my head.

12:05.850 --> 12:08.060
So a nice man in a big truck,

12:08.144 --> 12:10.187
he drove you to your mama's,
and then what?

12:10.271 --> 12:13.065
Your Aunt Becky gave you
those clothes and that makeup?

12:13.524 --> 12:14.483
I...

12:16.318 --> 12:17.653
I shouldn't have left.

12:20.906 --> 12:22.158
Mmm-mmm.

12:22.950 --> 12:23.909
No.

12:25.202 --> 12:27.746
No, this isn't on you, kid.
I should've been there.

12:30.833 --> 12:33.210
I should never have lied to you
about your mom.

12:34.295 --> 12:35.546
Or about when you could leave.

12:36.797 --> 12:38.549
A lot of things I shouldn't have done.

12:41.969 --> 12:43.387
Sometimes I feel like I'm...

12:46.974 --> 12:48.434
[inhales sharply]

12:48.517 --> 12:51.770
Like I'm just some kind of black hole
or something. [sighs]

12:51.854 --> 12:52.980
A black hole?

12:53.063 --> 12:56.775
Yeah, it's a...
You know, it's this thing in outer space.

12:56.859 --> 13:00.613
It's like, it sucks everything towards it
and destroys it.

13:01.614 --> 13:04.658
Sarah had a picture book
about outer space. She loved it.

13:05.618 --> 13:06.786
Who's Sarah?

13:07.369 --> 13:08.370
Sarah?

13:12.833 --> 13:14.251
Sarah's my girl.

13:17.630 --> 13:18.923
She's my little girl.

13:21.342 --> 13:22.426
Where is she?

13:23.969 --> 13:27.139
Well, that's kind of the thing, kid.
She, uh...

13:29.808 --> 13:31.143
She left us.

13:34.063 --> 13:35.898
- Gone.
- Yeah.

13:36.482 --> 13:39.318
The black hole. It got her.

13:43.239 --> 13:44.573
And somehow...

13:46.742 --> 13:48.661
I've just been scared, you know?

13:49.328 --> 13:52.122
I've just been scared
that it would take you, too.

13:53.541 --> 13:54.833
I think that's why I get...

13:56.085 --> 13:57.503
so mad.

14:00.756 --> 14:02.007
I'm so sorry.

14:03.801 --> 14:04.885
For everything.

14:07.221 --> 14:10.849
I could be so... so...

14:10.933 --> 14:12.184
Stupid?

14:12.268 --> 14:15.479
[chuckling] Yeah. Stupid.

14:15.563 --> 14:18.399
- [chuckles]
- Just really stupid.

14:28.659 --> 14:30.077
I've been stupid, too.

14:30.870 --> 14:32.746
I guess we broke our rule.

14:32.830 --> 14:33.914
[chuckles softly]

14:35.207 --> 14:37.001
I don't hate it, by the way.

14:37.084 --> 14:38.294
This whole...

14:39.920 --> 14:40.796
look.

14:43.007 --> 14:44.508
It's kinda cool.

14:46.010 --> 14:47.303
Bitchin'.

14:49.263 --> 14:51.140
Okay. Sure.

14:55.477 --> 14:58.772
- Bitchin'.
- [chuckles and sniffles]

15:13.704 --> 15:15.581
[monster roaring in distance]

15:26.133 --> 15:27.468
All right.

15:28.218 --> 15:29.887
[sighs] It should fit now.

15:30.763 --> 15:31.764
Is this really necessary?

15:31.847 --> 15:34.934
Yes, it is, okay? This is
a ground-breaking scientific discovery.

15:35.017 --> 15:38.354
We can't just bury it like
some common mammal, okay? It's not a dog.

15:38.437 --> 15:40.147
All right, all right, all right.

15:40.272 --> 15:43.025
But you're explaining this to Mrs. Byers,
all right?

15:44.318 --> 15:46.153
Christ. Help me out.

15:46.236 --> 15:48.280
- What am I supposed to do?
- Get the door, man.

15:48.364 --> 15:49.949
All right, I got the door.

15:50.032 --> 15:52.368
- Ew. Jesus--
- God--

15:54.036 --> 15:55.871
[panting]

15:55.955 --> 15:56.956
Phew!

16:08.050 --> 16:09.551
Mike, would you just stop already?

16:09.635 --> 16:11.178
You weren't in there, okay, Lucas?

16:11.261 --> 16:13.597
That lab is swarming
with hundreds of those dogs.

16:13.681 --> 16:15.808
- Demo-dogs!
- [Lucas] The chief will take care of her.

16:15.891 --> 16:17.142
Like she needs protection.

16:17.226 --> 16:19.019
Listen, dude,
a coach calls a play in a game,

16:19.103 --> 16:20.688
bottom line, you execute it. All right?

16:20.771 --> 16:22.982
Okay, first of all,
this isn't some stupid sports game.

16:23.065 --> 16:25.651
And second, we're not even in the game.
We're on the bench.

16:25.734 --> 16:28.112
[stammers] So my point is...

16:30.906 --> 16:33.826
Right, yeah, we're on the bench,
so, uh, there's nothing we can do.

16:33.909 --> 16:36.120
That's not entirely true.

16:36.203 --> 16:39.373
I mean, these Demo-dogs,
they have a hive mind.

16:39.456 --> 16:41.750
When they ran away from the bus,
they were called away.

16:41.834 --> 16:44.378
- If we get their attention...
- Maybe we can draw them from the lab.

16:44.461 --> 16:45.838
Clear a path to the gate.

16:45.921 --> 16:47.256
Yeah, and then we all die.

16:47.339 --> 16:48.340
That's one point of view.

16:48.424 --> 16:50.467
No, that's not a point of view, man.
That's a fact.

16:50.551 --> 16:51.885
I got it!

16:52.594 --> 16:56.223
This is where the chief dug his hole.
This is our way into the tunnel. So...

16:56.306 --> 16:58.517
Here, right here. This is like a hub.

16:58.600 --> 17:00.477
So you got all the tunnels
feeding in here.

17:00.561 --> 17:02.104
Maybe if we set this on fire...

17:02.187 --> 17:03.230
Oh, yeah? That's a no.

17:03.313 --> 17:05.941
- The mind flayer would call away his army.
- They'd all come to stop us.

17:06.025 --> 17:07.192
- We circle back to the exit.
- Guys.

17:07.276 --> 17:09.153
- By the time they realize we're gone--
- El would be at the gate.

17:09.236 --> 17:12.656
Hey. Hey! Hey! This is not happening.

17:12.740 --> 17:13.741
- But--
- No, no, no, no, no.

17:13.824 --> 17:15.743
No buts. I promised
I'd keep you shitheads safe,

17:15.826 --> 17:17.286
and that's exactly what I plan on.

17:17.369 --> 17:19.246
We're staying here. On the bench.

17:19.329 --> 17:21.540
And we're waiting for the starting team
to do their job.

17:21.623 --> 17:22.624
Does everybody understand?

17:22.708 --> 17:24.376
This isn't a stupid sports game.

17:24.460 --> 17:26.462
I said does everybody understand that?

17:27.588 --> 17:28.922
I need a yes.

17:30.215 --> 17:31.717
[engine revving]

17:34.762 --> 17:36.638
[rock music playing on car radio]

17:37.306 --> 17:38.474
[Max] It's my brother.

17:38.557 --> 17:41.977
He can't know I'm here.
He'll kill me. He'll kill us.

17:46.190 --> 17:47.649
[tires screech]

17:50.069 --> 17:51.278
[music stops playing]

17:57.326 --> 18:00.162
Am I dreaming, or is that you, Harrington?

18:00.245 --> 18:01.872
Yeah, it's me. Don't cream your pants.

18:03.248 --> 18:05.459
- [car door slams]
- What are you doing here, amigo?

18:06.085 --> 18:08.003
I could ask you the same thing.

18:08.921 --> 18:09.880
Amigo.

18:10.672 --> 18:14.426
Looking for my stepsister.
A little birdie told me she was here.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.178
Huh, that's weird. I don't know her.

18:16.261 --> 18:19.056
Small? Redhead? Bit of a bitch.

18:19.139 --> 18:20.516
Doesn't ring a bell. Sorry, buddy.

18:23.268 --> 18:25.437
[sighs] You know, I don't know, this...

18:26.021 --> 18:28.649
[clicks tongue] This whole situation,
Harrington, I don't know.

18:29.316 --> 18:30.651
It's giving me the heebie-jeebies.

18:30.734 --> 18:31.944
Oh, yeah? Why's that?

18:33.737 --> 18:36.532
My 13-year-old sister goes missing
all day.

18:36.615 --> 18:40.410
And then I find her with you
in a stranger's house.

18:42.037 --> 18:43.413
And you lie to me about it.

18:43.497 --> 18:44.790
[chuckles]

18:46.083 --> 18:48.710
Man, were you dropped too much
as a child, or what?

18:49.378 --> 18:52.339
I don't know what you don't understand
about what I just said.

18:54.174 --> 18:55.509
She's not here.

18:56.844 --> 18:57.970
Then who is that?

18:59.138 --> 19:01.890
[exclaims] Shit! Did he see us?

19:01.974 --> 19:03.642
Oh, shit. Listen--

19:05.352 --> 19:08.522
- I told you to plant your feet.
- [groans]

19:11.942 --> 19:13.235
Well, well, well.

19:14.862 --> 19:17.239
Lucas Sinclair. What a surprise.

19:18.532 --> 19:20.534
I thought I told you
to stay away from him, Max.

19:20.617 --> 19:22.494
- Billy, go away.
- You disobeyed me.

19:23.495 --> 19:25.372
And you know what happens
when you disobey me.

19:25.455 --> 19:27.708
- Billy...
- I break things. [grunts]

19:27.791 --> 19:31.378
- [indistinct yelling]
- Billy! Stop! Billy! Stop!

19:33.463 --> 19:34.464
Get off of me, you--

19:34.548 --> 19:36.842
Since Maxine won't listen to me,
maybe you will.

19:37.092 --> 19:38.719
You stay away from her.

19:38.802 --> 19:42.264
Stay away from her! You hear me?

19:43.140 --> 19:44.516
- I said get off me!
- [groans]

19:46.476 --> 19:49.646
So dead, Sinclair! You're dead.

19:50.939 --> 19:52.191
No. You are.

19:52.274 --> 19:53.275
- [groans]
- [chuckles]

19:53.358 --> 19:54.568
Steve!

19:54.651 --> 19:56.361
[laughing]

19:57.362 --> 20:00.490
Looks like you got some fire in you
after all, huh?

20:00.574 --> 20:02.409
I've been waiting to meet this King Steve

20:02.492 --> 20:05.704
everybody's been telling me so much about.

20:06.580 --> 20:07.581
Get out.

20:13.837 --> 20:15.631
- Yes! Kick his ass, Steve!
- [Mike] Get him!

20:15.714 --> 20:17.507
[Dustin] Murder the son of a bitch!

20:17.591 --> 20:19.551
- [Dustin] Now! Now!
- [Mike] Get that shithead!

20:19.635 --> 20:21.553
- [laughs]
- [Dustin] Kill the son of a bitch!

20:21.637 --> 20:22.763
- [Lucas] Steve!
- [Max] Billy!

20:23.222 --> 20:24.223
[Mike] Holy shit!

20:25.015 --> 20:27.017
- Shit!
- [Steve groans]

20:31.271 --> 20:34.691
- No one tells me what to do! [grunts]
- [groans]

20:35.150 --> 20:36.443
Whoo! Get up!

20:36.526 --> 20:38.403
- [kids yelling]
- [Dustin] You're gonna kill him.

20:39.446 --> 20:41.114
[inaudible]

21:02.636 --> 21:04.221
[Billy grunts]

21:04.304 --> 21:05.722
[gasping]

21:17.317 --> 21:18.819
The hell is this?

21:18.902 --> 21:20.988
[echoing] You little shit,
what did you do?

21:22.197 --> 21:23.490
What did you do?

21:25.284 --> 21:26.326
[Mike] Shit.

21:26.410 --> 21:28.245
[laughing]

21:33.917 --> 21:37.129
From here on out, you leave me
and my friends alone. Do you understand?

21:37.713 --> 21:38.964
Screw you.

21:42.718 --> 21:47.014
Say you understand! Say it! Say it!

21:47.931 --> 21:48.932
I understand.

21:49.016 --> 21:51.268
- What?
- I understand.

21:56.982 --> 21:58.400
[bat clatters]

22:05.365 --> 22:06.366
Let's get out of here.

22:39.649 --> 22:42.235
It's actually kinda nice.

22:49.618 --> 22:51.119
We'll do it here.

23:11.181 --> 23:13.183
Are you sure this is a good idea?

23:13.934 --> 23:16.061
This thing has had Will long enough.

23:17.521 --> 23:19.564
Let's kill the son of a bitch.

23:41.628 --> 23:42.712
[Hopper grunts]

23:51.930 --> 23:53.890
[monsters growling]

24:03.567 --> 24:05.068
- [snarls]
- Papa!

24:07.070 --> 24:08.071
[screams]

24:13.076 --> 24:16.872
All right. You let me do the heavy lifting
up front, all right?

24:16.955 --> 24:19.040
You save your strength till we're below.

24:21.501 --> 24:22.502
You okay?

24:36.766 --> 24:39.519
- [tires screeching]
- [engine revving]

24:47.027 --> 24:48.653
[liquid sloshing]

24:55.118 --> 24:56.411
Nancy?

25:00.123 --> 25:02.459
- [groaning]
- [Dustin] No, don't touch it.

25:04.252 --> 25:06.755
Hey, buddy... [shushing]

25:07.714 --> 25:09.174
It's okay. You put up a good fight.

25:09.257 --> 25:11.009
He kicked your ass,
but you put up a fight.

25:11.092 --> 25:12.302
- You're okay.
- [groans]

25:12.385 --> 25:15.055
[Lucas] Okay, you're gonna keep straight
for a half a mile,

25:15.138 --> 25:17.057
then make a left on Mount Sinai.

25:18.183 --> 25:19.851
[Steve] What's going on?

25:21.186 --> 25:22.270
Oh, my God!

25:22.354 --> 25:23.688
Just relax. She's driven before.

25:23.772 --> 25:25.273
- Yeah, in a parking lot.
- That counts.

25:25.357 --> 25:26.691
They were gonna leave you behind.

25:26.775 --> 25:27.901
Oh, my God.

25:27.984 --> 25:29.611
I promised that you'd be cool, okay?

25:29.694 --> 25:31.738
[Steve] Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
What's going on?

25:32.322 --> 25:37.244
Oh, my God. No! Whoa!
Stop the car. Slow down.

25:37.327 --> 25:39.246
- I told you he'd freak out.
- Stop the car!

25:39.329 --> 25:41.831
Everybody shut up! I'm trying to focus!

25:41.915 --> 25:43.541
Oh, wait, that's Mount Sinai. Make a left.

25:43.625 --> 25:45.043
- What?
- Make a left.

25:45.126 --> 25:47.379
- [tires screeching]
- [all screaming]

25:56.763 --> 25:57.847
[gasps]

26:02.227 --> 26:03.770
[breathing heavily]

26:04.354 --> 26:05.480
What's happening?

26:05.897 --> 26:07.649
[grunts] It hurts.

26:07.732 --> 26:13.905
[groaning and screaming]
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

26:14.572 --> 26:17.200
Let me go! Let me go! It hurts!

26:19.703 --> 26:23.373
It hurts! Let me go! Let me go! It hurts!

26:25.834 --> 26:27.168
- Mom.
- No!

26:28.253 --> 26:30.422
[screaming]

26:33.008 --> 26:36.011
Let me go! Let me go! Let me go!

26:37.012 --> 26:38.888
[engine revving]

26:44.060 --> 26:45.270
[yells] Hello!

26:45.353 --> 26:47.314
- [Dustin] Whoa!
- Incredible.

26:47.397 --> 26:49.399
I told you. Zoomer.

26:55.530 --> 26:56.740
[Steve groans]

26:57.782 --> 26:58.616
Guys.

27:02.078 --> 27:04.039
Oh, no. Guys.

27:05.457 --> 27:07.667
Hey, where do you think you're going?

27:07.751 --> 27:10.211
What are you, deaf? Hello?

27:10.295 --> 27:13.173
We are not going down there right now.
I made myself clear.

27:13.256 --> 27:16.009
Hey, there's no chance
we're going to that hole, all right?

27:16.092 --> 27:18.303
This ends right now!

27:18.386 --> 27:20.263
[Dustin] Steve, you're upset, I get it.

27:20.347 --> 27:23.975
But the bottom line is,
a party member requires assistance,

27:24.059 --> 27:26.936
and it is our duty
to provide that assistance.

27:27.020 --> 27:29.564
Now, I know you promised Nance
that you would keep us safe.

27:30.982 --> 27:32.359
So, keep us safe.

27:33.693 --> 27:34.694
[sighs]

27:36.946 --> 27:38.198
[Steve grunts]

27:40.742 --> 27:42.619
Holy shit.

27:46.414 --> 27:48.208
[Mike] Yeah,
I'm pretty sure it's this way.

27:48.291 --> 27:50.377
[Dustin] You're pretty sure,
or you're certain?

27:50.460 --> 27:53.338
[Mike] I'm 100% sure.
Just follow me and you'll know.

27:53.421 --> 27:56.174
[Steve] Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hey, hey, hey, hey. I don't think so.

27:56.257 --> 27:57.092
[Mike] What?

27:57.175 --> 28:01.429
Any of you little shits die down here,
I'm getting the blame. Got it, dipshit?

28:01.513 --> 28:04.682
From here on out, I'm leading the way.
Come on, let's go.

28:06.393 --> 28:07.394
Come on.

28:08.728 --> 28:09.854
Hey, a little hustle.

28:16.403 --> 28:18.196
[alarm blaring]

28:23.493 --> 28:25.412
[Hopper panting]

28:34.421 --> 28:35.630
Stay here.

28:43.596 --> 28:44.889
Oh, shit.

28:53.231 --> 28:54.357
Hey, Doc.

28:54.441 --> 28:56.067
[Owens sighs]

28:56.151 --> 28:59.028
[sighs] Those suckers
got you pretty good, huh?

28:59.696 --> 29:00.864
It's okay, don't talk.

29:01.573 --> 29:04.951
Don't talk. I got you.
I got you. I got you.

29:06.619 --> 29:07.787
[grunts]

29:08.955 --> 29:11.583
Oh, yeah, I've been meaning to tell you.

29:12.167 --> 29:16.337
This is Eleven. Eleven, Doc Owens.
Doc Owens, Eleven.

29:17.464 --> 29:20.967
She's been staying with me
for about a year

29:21.050 --> 29:23.428
and she's about to save our asses.

29:24.721 --> 29:26.264
Maybe when this is all said and done,

29:26.347 --> 29:28.892
maybe you could help her out, too,
you know?

29:29.517 --> 29:32.479
Maybe you could help her lead,
like, a normal life.

29:33.563 --> 29:35.982
One where she's not poked
and prodded and...

29:36.733 --> 29:38.943
treated like some kind of lab rat,
you know?

29:39.569 --> 29:40.779
I don't know, just a thought.

29:40.862 --> 29:42.447
[groans]

29:42.530 --> 29:45.408
But, uh... think about it.

29:52.207 --> 29:53.374
Don't go anywhere.

29:53.458 --> 29:54.709
[chuckles softly]

30:09.682 --> 30:10.892
[Lucas] God.

30:11.476 --> 30:13.353
[Max] What is this place?

30:13.436 --> 30:15.730
[Steve] Guys, come on. Keep moving.

30:22.737 --> 30:23.947
What the hell?

30:28.034 --> 30:30.203
[screaming] Shit!

30:33.122 --> 30:35.458
- Help! Help! Help!
- [Mike] Dustin.

30:35.542 --> 30:36.626
[Dustin] Shit!

30:36.709 --> 30:38.419
- [Lucas] Dustin!
- [Max] Dustin!

30:38.503 --> 30:39.629
[Steve] What happened?

30:39.712 --> 30:42.966
[whimpers] It's in my mouth!
Some got on my mouth! Shit!

30:43.049 --> 30:44.634
[coughing]

30:53.726 --> 30:54.853
I'm okay.

30:54.936 --> 30:57.355
- You serious?
- Very funny, man.

30:57.438 --> 30:59.440
- Nice. Very nice.
- Jesus, what an idiot.

31:00.233 --> 31:02.193
Hang on. Wait, wait.

31:10.827 --> 31:12.579
[Steve] All right, Wheeler.

31:13.872 --> 31:15.540
I think we found your hub.

31:29.012 --> 31:29.846
[Mike] Drench it.

31:41.524 --> 31:43.735
[screaming]

31:52.410 --> 31:56.247
It's not working. It's not working.
Mom, are you listening to me?

31:56.331 --> 31:58.207
- Just wait!
- How much longer?

31:58.291 --> 31:59.334
Look... look at him!

31:59.417 --> 32:00.877
- Jonathan, wait!
- You're killing him!

32:00.960 --> 32:02.253
[Joyce] Just wait!

32:03.129 --> 32:04.756
- No!
- No, leave it!

32:04.839 --> 32:05.882
- You're killing him!
- Leave it!

32:05.965 --> 32:09.844
Wait, Jonathan, Jonathan!
His neck! His neck!

32:10.470 --> 32:11.471
[choking]

32:19.896 --> 32:21.064
No, no, no, no.

32:41.167 --> 32:43.002
[monster roaring]

32:46.339 --> 32:47.548
Stay here.

32:51.678 --> 32:53.638
[breathing heavily]

32:57.266 --> 32:59.227
[growling]

33:39.475 --> 33:40.768
- [Steve] You ready?
- [Mike] Yeah.

33:40.852 --> 33:42.145
- [Lucas] Ready.
- [Max] Ready.

33:43.980 --> 33:45.148
[Dustin] Light her up.

33:46.274 --> 33:49.318
[Steve panting] I am in such deep shit.

33:50.653 --> 33:54.115
- [Will grunting]
- [Joyce choking]

34:05.168 --> 34:07.211
- [yelps]
- [gasping]

34:11.299 --> 34:12.133
All right.

34:21.642 --> 34:23.811
Get the hell out of my son!

34:31.486 --> 34:32.820
[screaming]

34:34.072 --> 34:35.823
[monsters shrieking]

34:40.620 --> 34:43.039
- [Steve] Go, go, go!
- [Dustin yelling]

34:44.749 --> 34:46.292
[shrieking]

34:49.879 --> 34:51.005
Let's go, let's go!

34:51.089 --> 34:52.215
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

34:52.298 --> 34:54.008
[all growling]

34:57.386 --> 34:59.263
[Will screaming]

35:23.663 --> 35:25.665
[Joyce crying] Will, baby.

35:26.332 --> 35:28.626
Will. Will.

35:28.709 --> 35:31.504
- Please, Will. Will.
- Come on, buddy.

35:31.587 --> 35:33.297
- Please. Can you hear me?
- Come on.

35:33.381 --> 35:35.299
- Come on.
- Please. Will.

35:35.967 --> 35:37.051
[Joyce gasps]

35:40.304 --> 35:41.430
Mom?

35:41.514 --> 35:44.642
- [gasps]
- Oh, honey. Oh, God.

36:05.371 --> 36:08.416
[Jonathan] Chief, are you there?
Chief, do you copy?

36:08.499 --> 36:09.375
Yeah, I copy.

36:09.458 --> 36:12.044
[panting] Close it.

36:50.208 --> 36:52.585
[Steve] Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

36:56.130 --> 36:57.340
Hey, this way!

36:59.592 --> 37:00.718
[Mike grunts]

37:01.594 --> 37:04.639
Help! Help! Help! Help!

37:56.649 --> 37:58.693
[Mike] Help! Help!

37:58.776 --> 38:00.778
- [Steve] Hold on!
- [Dustin] Steve, pull him out.

38:00.861 --> 38:02.405
[Lucas] Everybody back! Back!

38:02.488 --> 38:04.115
[Steve grunting]

38:08.536 --> 38:10.079
- [Lucas] You good?
- [Dustin] You okay?

38:10.162 --> 38:12.415
- [Steve] Guys, we gotta go!
- [Dart growling]

38:18.004 --> 38:19.171
[Dustin] Dart.

38:21.757 --> 38:22.883
[indistinct chatter]

38:22.967 --> 38:23.843
[Dustin] Shh. Stop.

38:23.926 --> 38:26.387
- [Max] Dustin, get back.
- [Dustin] Trust me, please.

38:30.349 --> 38:35.521
Hey. It's me, it's me.
It's just your friend, it's Dustin.

38:35.604 --> 38:37.398
It's Dustin, all right?

38:37.982 --> 38:39.317
You remember me?

38:41.152 --> 38:43.237
- Will you let us pass?
- [snarls]

38:44.613 --> 38:49.785
Okay, okay, I'm sorry.
I'm sorry about the storm cellar.

38:49.869 --> 38:51.912
That was a pretty douchey thing to do.

38:52.913 --> 38:55.833
You hungry? Yeah?

38:55.916 --> 38:57.126
- [Lucas] He's insane.
- [Mike] Don't.

38:57.209 --> 38:58.044
[Steve] Shut up.

38:58.127 --> 39:02.381
I've got our favorite. See? Nougat.

39:02.882 --> 39:03.716
[grunts]

39:06.344 --> 39:10.348
Look at that. Yummy. Here, all right?

39:10.431 --> 39:13.934
Eat up, buddy. Come on. Come on.

39:14.018 --> 39:15.102
[whispering] Let's go.

39:17.063 --> 39:19.190
There's plenty. I've got more.

39:22.860 --> 39:24.820
[Dart chomping and slurping]

39:33.162 --> 39:34.705
Goodbye, buddy.

39:35.831 --> 39:36.791
Let's go, let's go!

39:56.769 --> 39:58.771
[Kali] I want you to find something
from your past,

39:58.854 --> 40:00.147
something that angers you.

40:00.231 --> 40:01.440
Now channel it.

40:02.483 --> 40:03.901
[screams] Papa!

40:18.249 --> 40:19.542
[rumbling]

40:19.625 --> 40:20.626
Jesus!

40:21.710 --> 40:22.878
[monster roaring]

40:22.962 --> 40:23.921
[Max] What was that?

40:24.004 --> 40:25.631
[monster roaring]

40:26.882 --> 40:28.008
[Mike] They're coming.

40:28.551 --> 40:29.635
[Mike] Run! Run!

40:29.718 --> 40:30.594
Let's go! Let's go!

40:30.678 --> 40:32.430
Come on, Mike!
Move, Mike!

40:33.222 --> 40:35.975
- [Lucas] There, there!
- [Mike] Come on! Let's go.

40:36.058 --> 40:38.519
Go, go, go! Let's go!
Come on! Come on!

40:38.602 --> 40:39.603
- [Max grunts]
- Come on!

40:39.687 --> 40:41.313
Come on, hurry up! Come on!

40:41.397 --> 40:42.606
[panting]

40:44.733 --> 40:46.277
Come on, come on, come on!

40:46.360 --> 40:48.028
[Max] Lucas, come on.
Reach for my hand.

40:50.906 --> 40:52.032
[Lucas] Come on. Pull him.

40:52.116 --> 40:53.242
[monsters shriek]

40:53.325 --> 40:54.326
Oh, shit.

40:54.743 --> 40:55.786
[Steve] Here.

40:59.373 --> 41:01.250
Dustin! Come on!

41:02.835 --> 41:03.752
[Dustin] No!

41:03.836 --> 41:05.421
[gasps]

41:05.504 --> 41:06.881
[monsters growling]

41:10.301 --> 41:11.427
[Dustin] This is...

41:18.017 --> 41:19.018
Eleven.

41:38.913 --> 41:40.748
- [clanging]
- [gunfire]

41:49.590 --> 41:50.758
Oh, shit!

41:56.347 --> 41:57.389
[rifle clicks]

42:13.948 --> 42:15.407
You have a wound, Eleven.

42:17.076 --> 42:18.285
A terrible wound.

42:19.578 --> 42:21.455
The gate, I opened it.

42:22.873 --> 42:25.459
- [Dr. Brenner] And it's festering.
- [Eleven] I'm the monster.

42:26.377 --> 42:27.378
And it will grow.

42:31.048 --> 42:32.466
- Spread.
- [screams]

42:32.550 --> 42:33.676
Papa!

42:33.759 --> 42:34.593
[screaming]

42:36.554 --> 42:39.932
And eventually, it will kill you.

42:41.308 --> 42:43.394
- [screaming]
- Jane!

42:44.895 --> 42:47.189
[screaming]

43:07.459 --> 43:09.003
[continues screaming]

44:04.850 --> 44:06.268
[sniffles and cries]

44:06.352 --> 44:08.228
You did good, kid. [sighs]

44:09.938 --> 44:11.315
You did so good.

44:14.401 --> 44:16.111
[Hopper panting]

44:44.682 --> 44:46.684
[police radio chatter]

44:51.480 --> 44:53.482
[police radio chatter]

45:04.284 --> 45:06.578
[reporter] Since the release
of the incendiary tape, 

45:06.662 --> 45:09.123
the once quiet town of Hawkins, Indiana,

45:09.206 --> 45:11.917
has spent time in a place
it never expected.

45:12.000 --> 45:13.377
The national spotlight.

45:13.460 --> 45:14.878
[chuckles]

45:14.962 --> 45:17.756
[reporter] Under mounting pressure,
several high-ranking members

45:17.840 --> 45:19.216
from the U.S. Department of Energy 

45:19.299 --> 45:22.678
have admitted involvement
in the death and cover-up 

45:22.761 --> 45:25.889
of Hawkins resident Barbara Holland
who died due to exposure

45:25.973 --> 45:28.642
to an experimental chemical asphyxiant, 

45:28.725 --> 45:31.061
which had leaked
from the grounds of the lab.

45:31.145 --> 45:34.940
We sent our own April Kline to Hawkins
to speak to residents,

45:35.023 --> 45:38.819
residents who told us
they thought they lived in a safe town.

45:38.902 --> 45:42.739
The kind of town where,
they say, nothing ever happens.

45:55.419 --> 45:56.670
Chief-o.

45:56.753 --> 45:58.881
- How's the leg?
- Better.

45:58.964 --> 46:00.883
Pretty sure my football career is over.

46:00.966 --> 46:02.384
[both chuckle lightly]

46:02.468 --> 46:04.011
Want some? No way I'm gonna finish it.

46:04.094 --> 46:06.054
No. I'm, uh... on a diet.

46:06.138 --> 46:08.432
Well, you're a better man than me.

46:08.515 --> 46:11.101
- Hey, got a little something for you.
- [Hopper sighs]

46:21.778 --> 46:22.738
I thought--

46:22.821 --> 46:24.239
Sometimes I impress even myself.

46:24.990 --> 46:27.451
Still, I'd let things cool off
for a while, if I were you.

46:27.534 --> 46:29.661
How long is a while? [sniffles]

46:30.537 --> 46:31.872
Want to be safe? I give it a year.

46:31.955 --> 46:32.956
A year?

46:38.420 --> 46:39.421
What about one night out?

46:39.505 --> 46:40.547
One night?

46:40.631 --> 46:42.925
Yeah. How risky would that be?

46:43.008 --> 46:44.801
What's so important about one night?

46:52.684 --> 46:56.146
♪ Jingle bell, jingle bell
Jingle bell rock ♪

46:56.230 --> 47:00.150
♪ Jingle bells chime in jingle bell time ♪

47:00.943 --> 47:04.363
[Joyce] Yeah, you got it. See?

47:04.446 --> 47:05.822
[Will] Mom!

47:06.657 --> 47:08.742
[Joyce laughs] Wow!

47:08.825 --> 47:11.203
♪ Jingle bell, jingle bell
Jingle bell rock ♪

47:11.286 --> 47:14.790
♪ Jingle bells chime in jingle bell time ♪

47:15.791 --> 47:17.626
Do you always
have to be filming everything?

47:17.709 --> 47:20.128
No, no. Just the good stuff. [chuckles]

47:20.212 --> 47:22.339
Are you sure people still dance like this?

47:22.422 --> 47:24.383
Yeah. It's just what's happening.

47:24.466 --> 47:25.634
Is it what's happening?

47:25.717 --> 47:27.636
Yeah, yeah, it's what's happening.

47:30.389 --> 47:31.640
[camera shutter clicks]

47:33.100 --> 47:33.934
Oh, wait.

47:34.017 --> 47:35.227
All right, that's enough.

47:35.310 --> 47:37.688
- One more, okay? Just one more.
- Why?

47:37.771 --> 47:39.565
- You look so handsome.
- Mom!

47:39.648 --> 47:40.607
Mike.

47:42.109 --> 47:44.945
- ♪ Jingle around the clock ♪
- Hey... wanna dance?

47:45.028 --> 47:47.030
- ♪ Mix and a-mingle... ♪
- No.

47:47.114 --> 47:52.578
We should, you know, get out there,
like, do our thing... Stop.

47:52.661 --> 47:56.164
♪ Jingle bell, jingle bell
Jingle bell rock ♪

47:56.248 --> 47:58.208
- ♪ Jingle bells chime ♪
- I love this song.

47:58.292 --> 47:59.918
- ♪ In jingle bell time ♪
- You?

48:00.002 --> 48:04.298
Yeah, I love it.
But not as much as I love you, Lukey.

48:04.881 --> 48:06.675
- Get out of my room!
- [door slams]

48:06.758 --> 48:08.927
- Ow, ow. That hurts.
- [song continues]

48:09.011 --> 48:10.846
It's gonna be worth it. Promise.

48:10.929 --> 48:13.140
- ♪ To rock the night away ♪
- [Susan sighs]

48:14.558 --> 48:18.395
♪ Jingle bell time is a swell time ♪

48:18.979 --> 48:21.398
- ♪ To go gliding in a one-horse sleigh ♪
- See? Pretty.

48:21.481 --> 48:25.694
- Son of a bitch! Son of a bitch!
- ♪ Giddy-up jingle horse... ♪

48:25.777 --> 48:27.321
Where did you see it last?

48:27.404 --> 48:28.530
Right here, where I put it.

48:28.614 --> 48:30.782
What's in there
that's so important anyway?

48:31.366 --> 48:33.160
You look fabulous, baby.

48:34.328 --> 48:35.787
- ♪ That's the jingle bell ♪
- Got it.

48:35.871 --> 48:37.372
♪ That's the jingle bell.. ♪

48:37.456 --> 48:40.334
- [doorbell rings]
- That's your ride. Dusty!

48:42.336 --> 48:43.295
[song ends]

48:46.715 --> 48:48.508
[exhales] Okay.

49:01.104 --> 49:03.273
All right, buddy, here we are.

49:04.399 --> 49:05.984
So, remember, once you get in there...

49:07.235 --> 49:08.236
Pretend like I don't care.

49:08.320 --> 49:09.613
- You don't care.
- I don't care.

49:09.696 --> 49:12.032
There you go. You're learning, my friend.
You're learning.

49:13.700 --> 49:14.576
- Hey.
- What?

49:14.660 --> 49:18.288
Come on. You look great, okay?
You look... You look great.

49:18.372 --> 49:20.999
- Okay? Now you're gonna go in there...
- Yeah.

49:21.083 --> 49:22.834
- Look like a million bucks.
- Yeah.

49:22.918 --> 49:24.211
And you're gonna slay 'em dead.

49:24.294 --> 49:25.796
Like a lion.

49:25.879 --> 49:27.297
[purrs]

49:28.548 --> 49:29.925
Don't do that, okay?

49:30.008 --> 49:31.176
Okay.

49:32.719 --> 49:33.929
Good luck.

49:39.351 --> 49:41.478
[dance music playing]

49:41.978 --> 49:43.063
[exhales]

49:47.609 --> 49:50.946
- Looking very snazzy tonight, sir.
- Thank you, my lord.

50:33.780 --> 50:36.324
- Hey, Nance.
- Hey.

50:37.743 --> 50:40.871
- What's in this?
- Pure fuel.

50:53.884 --> 50:55.510
Holy shit. What happened to you?

50:56.344 --> 50:58.555
- What do you mean, "What happened"?
- What?

50:58.638 --> 50:59.473
- Dude.
- Your hair.

50:59.556 --> 51:01.016
Is there a bird nesting in there?

51:01.099 --> 51:02.684
What do you mean, "What's wrong"?

51:02.768 --> 51:05.187
There's no bird nesting in here, asshole.
Okay?

51:05.270 --> 51:06.354
I worked hard.

51:06.438 --> 51:08.648
[slow romantic song playing]

51:12.944 --> 51:14.112
[exhales]

51:14.738 --> 51:15.572
Max...

51:16.865 --> 51:18.033
Hey.

51:18.658 --> 51:20.202
Um, it's nice, right?

51:20.285 --> 51:21.578
You want to, um...

51:22.496 --> 51:23.872
You want to, like... You know?

51:23.955 --> 51:26.750
Like, just you and me?

51:27.793 --> 51:29.544
Are you trying
to ask me to dance, stalker?

51:30.003 --> 51:32.005
No, of course not.

51:32.464 --> 51:34.466
- Unless you want to.
- [chuckles]

51:34.549 --> 51:36.301
So smooth. Come on.

51:48.188 --> 51:49.856
[girl] Hey, Zombie Boy.

51:50.524 --> 51:51.525
Do you want to dance?

51:51.608 --> 51:53.485
[stammering] Um... I don't...

51:54.778 --> 51:57.114
- I mean... I mean, yeah. Sure.
- Cool.

52:20.846 --> 52:24.516
[exhales] Wish me luck, Mike.
I'm going in.

52:24.599 --> 52:25.559
[clicks tongue]

52:30.146 --> 52:31.773
[indistinct chatter]

52:31.857 --> 52:34.276
- [clears throat] Stacy.
- He just broke up with Jennifer.

52:34.359 --> 52:37.279
- Plus he's, like, not my type.
- [clears throat] Stacy.

52:39.990 --> 52:40.866
Yeah?

52:40.949 --> 52:42.534
[clears throat]

52:43.827 --> 52:44.828
Shall we?

52:46.204 --> 52:48.623
- Um, no, thanks. [chuckles]
- [girls laugh]

52:58.717 --> 53:00.051
[exhales]

53:01.803 --> 53:02.929
Oh, my God.

53:40.675 --> 53:43.511
- Hey.
- Hey.

53:45.013 --> 53:47.349
- Wanna dance?
- What?

53:47.807 --> 53:49.559
Come on. Let's go.

53:58.193 --> 54:00.779
Here. Mmm-hmm.

54:02.030 --> 54:03.031
Closer.

54:04.741 --> 54:07.118
A little closer. Okay.

54:08.244 --> 54:10.705
Now feel the music.

54:10.789 --> 54:12.415
The rhythm.

54:12.499 --> 54:15.210
Start to move to it.

54:15.293 --> 54:17.087
Yeah. There.

54:17.170 --> 54:18.672
- Good?
- That's good. Yeah.

54:18.755 --> 54:19.839
Okay.

54:19.923 --> 54:23.260
You know,
out of all of my brother's friends,

54:23.927 --> 54:24.928
you're my favorite.

54:26.304 --> 54:28.598
- You've always been my favorite.
- Really?

54:28.682 --> 54:29.683
Yeah. [chuckles]

54:32.811 --> 54:34.771
[girls murmuring]

54:34.854 --> 54:37.899
Girls this age are dumb.

54:37.983 --> 54:41.569
But give them a few years,
and they'll wise up.

54:42.445 --> 54:45.365
And, uh, you're gonna drive them nuts.

54:45.448 --> 54:48.827
- You think so?
- Oh, I know so. [chuckles]

55:03.258 --> 55:05.593
- Hey.
- Hey.

55:06.469 --> 55:08.471
Thought I might find you out here.

55:09.180 --> 55:12.934
Will wanted me to give him
some space, so...

55:13.685 --> 55:15.228
I'm giving him a few feet. [chuckles]

55:17.355 --> 55:18.690
What do you say?

55:19.733 --> 55:24.946
I'm pretty sure that Mr. Cooper retired
in the '70s, so...

55:26.406 --> 55:28.199
we might be okay.

55:32.996 --> 55:34.831
[inhales sharply]

55:40.170 --> 55:41.421
[coughs]

55:44.424 --> 55:45.592
How are you holding up?

55:46.634 --> 55:48.178
- You know.
- Yeah.

55:48.762 --> 55:50.430
That feeling never goes away.

55:52.223 --> 55:54.142
It is true what they say, you know.

55:55.477 --> 55:57.479
Every day it does get a little easier.

56:21.461 --> 56:24.547
♪ Every breath you take ♪

56:25.423 --> 56:28.468
♪ Every move you make ♪

56:29.636 --> 56:33.598
♪ Every bond you break
Every step you take ♪

56:33.681 --> 56:36.059
♪ I'll be watching you ♪

56:37.811 --> 56:41.773
♪ Every single day ♪

56:41.856 --> 56:44.901
♪ Every word you say ♪

56:46.778 --> 56:47.862
You look beautiful.

56:50.949 --> 56:52.075
Do you wanna dance?

56:54.327 --> 56:56.412
I don't know how.

56:56.913 --> 56:58.081
I don't either.

56:58.498 --> 56:59.999
Do you want to figure it out?

57:02.544 --> 57:05.964
♪ My poor heart aches ♪

57:06.422 --> 57:09.134
♪ With every step you take ♪

57:09.217 --> 57:10.635
Like this.

57:11.094 --> 57:12.887
Yeah, like that.

57:14.889 --> 57:17.267
♪ Every vow you break ♪

57:18.685 --> 57:22.397
♪ Every smile you fake
Every claim you stake ♪

57:22.480 --> 57:24.858
♪ I'll be watching you ♪

57:28.778 --> 57:32.824
♪ Since you've gone
I been lost without a trace ♪

57:32.907 --> 57:36.995
♪ I dream at night
I can only see your face ♪

57:37.078 --> 57:41.166
♪ I look around
But it's you I can't replace ♪

57:41.249 --> 57:45.211
♪ I feel so cold
And I long for your embrace ♪

57:45.295 --> 57:51.301
♪ I keep crying baby, baby, please ♪

58:08.902 --> 58:11.821
[song fading]

58:44.979 --> 58:46.981
[theme music playing]
